MID_SE_Hur_Cen_C: <EDH>
MID_SE_Hur_Cen_C_001: Ultand! A moment, please? I'd like to ask\nyou something.
MID_SE_Hur_Cen_C_002: Oh! Um, of course. Am I in trouble?
MID_SE_Hur_Cen_C_003: No, no. Don't worry. It's nothing bad.
MID_SE_Hur_Cen_C_004: I'm thinking of recommending you as a new vulkan.
MID_SE_Hur_Cen_C_005: What?! You think I'm ready for that?
MID_SE_Hur_Cen_C_006: I take care of Aurora, sure, but that's not the same as\nbeing in a god's elite guard.
MID_SE_Hur_Cen_C_007: I know you don't see it, but you've more than\nproven yourself.
MID_SE_Hur_Cen_C_008: You're an expert in sacred magic. You've endured my\ntraining and forged excellent spear skills.
MID_SE_Hur_Cen_C_009: And on top of all that, you possess the most\nimportant trait you need for this duty.
MID_SE_Hur_Cen_C_010: And...what's that?
MID_SE_Hur_Cen_C_011: As a personal attendant to Aurora, you've shown a\nsincere loyalty, have you not?
MID_SE_Hur_Cen_C_012: Yes! My loyalty is unquestionable!
MID_SE_Hur_Cen_C_013: Which is precisely why I know that you should\nbecome a vulkan.
MID_SE_Hur_Cen_C_014: After the Heroic Games, there will be openings for\nnew candidates. I'll put your name in myself.
MID_SE_Hur_Cen_C_016: Centurio... I don't know what to say.
MID_SE_Hur_Cen_C_017: It's just... You've scolded me so often. I'm a little\nstunned by all of this.
MID_SE_Hur_Cen_C_018: It's my job to correct you, and sometimes you need\ncorrection. But I do appreciate you very much.
MID_SE_Hur_Cen_C_019: In matters of Aurora's comfort and safety, you speak\nboldly, even to me, your chief celestial general.
MID_SE_Hur_Cen_C_020: I know. I've made mistakes. But getting these\ncompliments from you makes me very happy.
MID_SE_Hur_Cen_C_021: I intend to train that much more now, so don't take it\neasy on me.
MID_SE_Hur_Cen_C_022: I won't.
MID_SE_Hur_Cen_C_023: But not so fast. I interrupted you earlier. Weren't you\nin the middle of something?
MID_SE_Hur_Cen_C_024: Oh! Right! I was getting water for Aurora.
MID_SE_Hur_Cen_C_025: One of the snacks I got her at the market was\nsurprisingly spicy!
MID_SE_Hur_Cen_C_026: Ultand! GO! And don't offer food to gods that you\nhaven't tested yourself!
MID_SE_Hur_Cen_C_027: Y-yes, Sir! I'm so sorry! I'll, uh, talk to you about\ntraining some other time.
MID_SE_Hur_Cen_C_028: She's got a good heart, but I doubt she'll become less\ncareless when she's a vulkan.